Residential & Bespoke Projects Limited (commercially trading under the same name or associated with RNB Construction Ltd) is an established high-end residential builder and construction firm based in Auckland. Founded in February 2021, the firm positions itself as a specialized "quality-over-quantity" operation catering to clients with premium visions, architectural requirements, and custom new builds. [1, 2, 3, 4, 5]
The company operates out of its primary commercial hub located at 66B Morrin Road, St Johns, Auckland 1072. [1]

Company Leadership & Shareholder Structure

According to filings managed via the New Zealand Companies Office, the governance and structural ownership of the firm are clearly split between its two executive founders: [1, 2]
Troy Boucher (Director / Co-Founder): Holds direct administrative and executive control as a primary registered director. [1]
Brett Armstrong (Director / Co-Founder): Shares equal corporate governance, acting alongside Boucher as the secondary registered director. [1]
The Shareholder Mix: While both men serve as the day-to-day operational directors, the capital framework features outside corporate tracking mechanisms. A designated block of the company's equity (recorded at 20%) is structurally allocated to Taonga Corporate Trustee Limited, a protective vehicle often utilized in New Zealand corporate architecture to hold equity on behalf of family interests or private trusts. [1]


Where They Live, Eat, and Socialise

Because Residential & Bespoke Projects Limited is a privately held enterprise, specific personal details such as the founders' private residential addresses, exact dining locations, personal hobbies, and social circles are kept confidential and are not a matter of public corporate record.
However, their active high-end professional footprint dictates their geographic and social lifestyle circles across Auckland:
Where They Operate & Live: Professionally, the team is anchored in the St Johns / Eastern Bays light-industrial precinct. Geographically, their high-spec residential construction projects dictate their daily movements. The firm builds heavily across the premium coastal strips of Auckland—frequently operating on multi-million dollar architectural footprints in Takapuna on the North Shore, waterfront properties across the East Auckland bays, and high-end coastal holiday builds in the Coromandel. [1, 2, 3, 4]
What They Do & Where They Eat: As hands-on, master-class building directors managing premium architectural builds, their daily routines are spent directly on-site coordinating structural steel, framing, and finishing details. Socially, their localized presence heavily features classic Auckland building industry lifestyle markers—such as winding down directly on-site overlooking the water with a post-handover beer or celebrating major milestone sign-offs over wine and coastal dining options near their active premium waterfront zones. [1]
Their Friends & Professional Networks: The founders' "social" network is heavily defined by high-tier professional alliances in the New Zealand luxury housing ecosystem. They maintain close working circles with premier architectural teams, structural consultants, and top-tier designers—such as Smith Architects, MSC Consulting Engineers, and Trinity Interior Design—collaborating directly with affluent private clients who have the capital to fund bespoke 400m²+ luxury builds. They are also closely aligned with industry regulatory networks, maintaining active ties to the Registered Master Builders Association and Licensed Building Practitioners networks.
